{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My soul is weary of my life;\nI will give free course to my complaint;\nI will speak in the bitterness of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will say unto God, Do not condemn me;\nShow me wherefore thou contendest with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it good unto thee that thou shouldest oppress,\nThat thou shouldest despise the work of thy hands,\nAnd shine upon the counsel of the wicked?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou eyes of flesh?\nOr seest thou as man seeth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are thy days as the days of man,\nOr thy years as man’s days,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou inquirest after mine iniquity,\nAnd searchest after my sin,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Although thou knowest that I am not wicked,\nAnd there is none that can deliver out of thy hand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy hands have framed me and fashioned me\nTogether round about; yet thou dost destroy me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember, I beseech thee, that thou hast fashioned me as clay;\nAnd wilt thou bring me into dust again?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou not poured me out as milk,\nAnd curdled me like cheese?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast clothed me with skin and flesh,\nAnd knit me together with bones and sinews.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast granted me life and lovingkindness;\nAnd thy visitation hath preserved my spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet these things thou didst hide in thy heart;\nI know that this is with thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I sin, then thou markest me,\nAnd thou wilt not acquit me from mine iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I be wicked, woe unto me;\nAnd if I be righteous, yet shall I not lift up my head;Being filled with ignominy,\nAnd looking upon mine affliction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my head",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " exalt itself, thou huntest me as a lion;\nAnd again thou showest thyself marvellous upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou renewest thy witnesses against me,\nAnd increasest thine indignation upon me:Changes and warfare are with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore then hast thou brought me forth out of the womb?\nI had given up the ghost, and no eye had seen me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I should have been as though I had not been;\nI should have been carried from the womb to the grave.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are not my days few? cease then,\nAnd let me alone, that I may take comfort a little,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before I go whence I shall not return,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the land of darkness and of the shadow of death;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.10.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.10.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The land dark as midnight,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "The land",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the shadow of death, without any order,\nAnd where the light is as midnight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
